00:24:57.050 --> 00:25:00.770
OK, so the first one is everyone
knows what a hyperplane is.

00:25:00.770 --> 00:25:03.080
So a hyperplane is--

00:25:03.080 --> 00:25:06.080
it's the set-- actually,
it's the solution set

00:25:06.080 --> 00:25:09.980
of a single non-zero
linear equation.

00:25:09.980 --> 00:25:12.200
That's what a hyperplane is.

00:25:12.200 --> 00:25:14.030
And you know what a
hyperplane looks like.

00:25:14.030 --> 00:25:17.280
In two-dimensions,
it looks like this.

00:25:17.280 --> 00:25:18.830
Here's a hyperplane there.

00:25:18.830 --> 00:25:22.130
Everything on that
line satisfies

00:25:22.130 --> 00:25:24.140
a two-dimensional equation.

00:25:24.140 --> 00:25:27.320
Sorry, a single equation
in two variables.

00:25:27.320 --> 00:25:28.340
So that's what it means.

00:25:28.340 --> 00:25:31.880
And in 3D space, it's actually
literally a hyperplane--

00:25:31.880 --> 00:25:33.320
it's a plane.

00:25:33.320 --> 00:25:35.510
And then, in higher
dimensions, it's

00:25:35.510 --> 00:25:36.890
what people call a hyperplane.

00:25:36.890 --> 00:25:39.350
OK, so that's that.

00:25:39.350 --> 00:25:41.990
That's just linear algebra.

00:25:41.990 --> 00:25:43.670
Now let's make it
interesting and make

00:25:43.670 --> 00:25:46.410
it-- let's make it asymmetric.

00:25:46.410 --> 00:25:48.730
So this is called a halfspace.

00:25:48.730 --> 00:25:51.060
So what happens is if--
it's the set of points,

00:25:51.060 --> 00:25:54.540
not that have a transpose x
equals b, but a transpose x

00:25:54.540 --> 00:25:56.180
is less than or equal to b.

00:25:56.180 --> 00:25:59.190
So that's a-- actually,
it's the solution

00:25:59.190 --> 00:26:03.930
set of a single non-zero
linear inequality.

00:26:03.930 --> 00:26:05.910
OK, that's what you
would call this.

00:26:05.910 --> 00:26:07.920
And that's a halfspace.

00:26:07.920 --> 00:26:09.180
And it looks like this.

00:26:09.180 --> 00:26:12.960
Roughly speaking, these
are all the points

00:26:12.960 --> 00:26:16.260
where a transpose x equals b.

00:26:16.260 --> 00:26:18.690
These are all the points
where a transpose x is bigger

00:26:18.690 --> 00:26:21.180
than b, and here's
where a transpose x is

00:26:21.180 --> 00:26:22.335
less than or equal to b.

00:26:22.335 --> 00:26:24.030
So that's the idea.

00:26:24.030 --> 00:26:27.180
And there's a lot of ways to
think of it geometrically.

00:26:27.180 --> 00:26:33.330
One way is to say, so here,
a is the outward normal

00:26:33.330 --> 00:26:34.980
of that halfspace.

00:26:34.980 --> 00:26:36.090
That's what people say.

00:26:36.090 --> 00:26:40.380
Normal means it's perpendicular
to the hyperplane.

00:26:40.380 --> 00:26:44.280
Outward means it points
out, so it's oriented.

00:26:44.280 --> 00:26:47.040
And you don't have concepts
like outward in linear algebra.

00:26:47.040 --> 00:26:50.550
You just have equality
constraints and subspace,

00:26:50.550 --> 00:26:51.480
the affine sets.

00:26:51.480 --> 00:26:52.365
Yes.

00:26:52.365 --> 00:26:59.000
[INAUDIBLE] have to be
1 to be a normal vector?

00:26:59.000 --> 00:27:00.170
Say that again, what?

00:27:00.170 --> 00:27:03.440
Is the magnitude of
a it has to be 1?

00:27:03.440 --> 00:27:04.190
No.

00:27:04.190 --> 00:27:08.380
So, like, if it is not 1,
it's pretty much [INAUDIBLE]..

00:27:08.380 --> 00:27:11.480
No, if something like
that is required,

00:27:11.480 --> 00:27:15.760
I'm going to tell you I'm a kind
of a full-disclosure person.

00:27:15.760 --> 00:27:17.980
So there's not going to
be anything hidden here

00:27:17.980 --> 00:27:20.500
like, oh, I didn't tell you a
is nonnegative or something.

00:27:20.500 --> 00:27:22.987
So no, a is a completely
general coefficient.

00:27:22.987 --> 00:27:25.195
The norm can be anything
you like, it doesn't matter.

00:27:28.420 --> 00:27:32.320
OK, so hyperplanes,
they're affine sets.

00:27:32.320 --> 00:27:36.730
Oh, by the way, any
affine set is convex.

00:27:36.730 --> 00:27:40.150
Halfspaces are convex.

00:27:40.150 --> 00:27:41.500
It's getting-- don't worry.

00:27:41.500 --> 00:27:43.120
It starts this starts slow.

00:27:43.120 --> 00:27:44.690
But trust me, by
