00:27:50.980 --> 00:27:57.970
OK, next up are Euclidean
balls and ellipsoids.

00:27:57.970 --> 00:28:00.390
So in this class,
it is a little.

00:28:00.390 --> 00:28:01.940
It's a step up mathematically.

00:28:01.940 --> 00:28:05.540
So we use the standard notation,
is that when we have a norm,

00:28:05.540 --> 00:28:07.580
if it's a sub 2 that
means the Euclidean norm.

00:28:07.580 --> 00:28:09.560
It's the square root of
the sum of the squares.

00:28:09.560 --> 00:28:12.320
If it doesn't have a 2
there, it's a generic norm.

00:28:12.320 --> 00:28:13.160
It's any norm.

00:28:13.160 --> 00:28:14.430
We'll get to that in a minute.

00:28:14.430 --> 00:28:16.493
But that's how we're
